%# expected-result: FAIL
%description:

Tests where an 802.1Q tag inserter takes the PCP of its tag from, in three steps.
Step 1 maps a user priority request to a PCP request of the tag type, unless the
packet already has one (mapUserPriorityReqToPcpReq), and removes the user
priority request if removeUserPriorityReq is set; otherwise the request stays on
the packet for the layers below (IEEE 802.1Q-2018 6.9.2). Step 2 takes the PCP
from the PCP request, or from defaultPcp; -1 leaves the PCP unspecified: the tag
gets PCP 0 and the packet no PCP indication. Step 3 indicates the PCP of the tag
as the user priority of the frame (mapPcpIndToUserPriorityInd).

Each chain sends packets with the requests that its requester lists per packet
through one C-tag inserter to a probe:
- a: default parameters; a user priority, a user priority overridden by a PCP
  request, no request, and a PCP request alone
- b: mapUserPriorityReqToPcpReq = false and defaultPcp = 4; the user priority
  request is ignored and stays on the packet
- c: removeUserPriorityReq = true; the user priority request is removed, also
  when a PCP request overrides it
- d: mapPcpIndToUserPriorityInd = false; no user priority indication
- e: defaultPcp = 5 and no request
- f: an invalid user priority (9) that a PCP request overrides is not used, so it
  is not rejected, and stays on the packet

%file: test.ned

import inet.test.moduletest.lib.PcpTestChain;

network Test
{
    submodules:
        a: PcpTestChain;
        b: PcpTestChain;
        c: PcpTestChain;
        d: PcpTestChain;
        e: PcpTestChain;
        f: PcpTestChain;
}

%inifile: omnetpp.ini

[General]
network = Test
ned-path = .;../../../../src;../../lib
sim-time-limit = 3.5s
cmdenv-express-mode = false
cmdenv-event-banners = false
**.cmdenv-log-level = off
*.a.requester.userPriorities = [6, 6, -1, -1]
*.a.requester.cPcps = [-1, 3, -1, 2]
*.b.requester.userPriorities = [6]
*.b.cInserter.mapUserPriorityReqToPcpReq = false
*.b.cInserter.defaultPcp = 4
*.c.requester.userPriorities = [6, 6]
*.c.requester.cPcps = [-1, 3]
*.c.cInserter.removeUserPriorityReq = true
*.d.requester.userPriorities = [6]
*.d.cInserter.mapPcpIndToUserPriorityInd = false
*.e.cInserter.defaultPcp = 5
*.f.requester.userPriorities = [9]
*.f.requester.cPcps = [3]

%contains: stdout
a #0: pcp0=6 UserPriorityReq=6 UserPriorityInd=6 CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=6 SPcpInd=none

%contains: stdout
a #1: pcp0=3 UserPriorityReq=6 UserPriorityInd=3 CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=3 SPcpInd=none

%contains: stdout
a #2: pcp0=0 UserPriorityReq=none UserPriorityInd=none CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=none SPcpInd=none

%contains: stdout
a #3: pcp0=2 UserPriorityReq=none UserPriorityInd=2 CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=2 SPcpInd=none

%contains: stdout
b #0: pcp0=4 UserPriorityReq=6 UserPriorityInd=4 CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=4 SPcpInd=none

%contains: stdout
c #0: pcp0=6 UserPriorityReq=none UserPriorityInd=6 CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=6 SPcpInd=none

%contains: stdout
c #1: pcp0=3 UserPriorityReq=none UserPriorityInd=3 CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=3 SPcpInd=none

%contains: stdout
d #0: pcp0=6 UserPriorityReq=6 UserPriorityInd=none CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=6 SPcpInd=none

%contains: stdout
e #0: pcp0=5 UserPriorityReq=none UserPriorityInd=5 CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=5 SPcpInd=none

%contains: stdout
f #0: pcp0=3 UserPriorityReq=9 UserPriorityInd=3 CPcpReq=none SPcpReq=none CPcpInd=3 SPcpInd=none
